  "releaseNotes": "2025-05-08\n - Updates to match the current stable Chromium and Chrome browsers (~136.0+)\n - Auto detects Windows, Linux, MacOS environment and adjusts accordingly\n - Allows for headless = false to be more easily used\n - Additional constructors and Unit testing to use a pre-existing chrome/chromium process for testing\n - Fixed output to better match cross platform and cross environment messaging requirements (docker vs. windows, etc)\nv1.4.9\n - Fix namespace mismatches in implementations\nv1.4.8\n - Modernize to current Google Chrome/Chromium 4/23/2025",
